# {{lb|en|nautical}} A small, strong triangular [[sail]] sometimes [[set]] in place of the [[mainsail]] in [[heavy weather]].
#* {{quote-book|en|1914|Jack London|The Mutiny of the Elsinore|section=[[s:The Mutiny of the Elsinore/Chapter XLIV|Chapter XLIV]]|passage=I have worked like a Trojan all day, and the idea is realized. Margaret helped me out with suggestions, and Tom Spink did the sailorizing. Over our head, from the jiggermast, the steel stays that carry the three jigger-'''trysails''' descend high above the break of the poop and across the main deck to the mizzenmast.}}

